From f369d19ecbcbc1be618433ff5d8e264f0c95fe11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:23:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: text anti-aliasing strength options (Off / On / Crisp /
 Dark)

Text Anti-Aliasing grows from a toggle into a 4-value enum. Values 0/1 keep
the legacy Off/On meaning so persisted settings from older builds round-trip
unchanged; the new strengths append (same append-only rule as
LONG_PRESS_MENU_FUNCTION).

The panel's grayscale pipeline offers exactly two gray targets per pixel
(MSB plane only = light gray, MSB+LSB = dark gray) over a BW base that
paints every non-white glyph pixel black, and the 2-bit fonts carry exactly
two edge levels. A strength therefore is a mapping from glyph edge level to
plane membership, applied in renderCharImpl's grayscale branches:

  On (Standard): glyph dark -> panel dark, glyph light -> panel light
  Crisp:         glyph dark -> black,      glyph light -> panel light
  Dark:          glyph dark -> black,      glyph light -> panel dark

These are the only distinct monotone mappings the hardware supports; going
lighter than Standard is impossible because planes can only lighten pixels
the BW base already painted black. The mapping lives on GfxRenderer as
renderer state (GrayscaleAaStrength, parallel to RenderMode) so reader
activities set it once from SETTINGS; image rendering (drawBitmap) keeps its
fixed mapping, and the BW pass is untouched byte-for-byte, so AA Off output
is identical to before.

UI: the Text Settings Style row cycles Off -> On -> Crisp -> Dark; the web
settings API serves the same values as an enum under the unchanged
textAntiAliasing key. New builds load old 0/1 files as-is; old builds clamp
the new values back to their default (AA on).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011Y2uNauEmkUi5Fs5Sa573x
